

**12. Struve Functions and Related Functions**

**Mathematical Properties**

### 12.1 Struve Function H,(z) Differential Equation and General Solution

\[z^{2}\frac{d^{3}w}{dz^{2}}+z\frac{dw}{dz}+(z^{2}->^{2})w=\frac{4(3z)^{\gamma+1}}{\sqrt{\pi}\Gamma(v-\frac{1}{2})}\]

The general solution is

#### 12.1.2 \(w=aJ_{v}(z)+bY_{v}(z)+\mathbf{H}_{v}(z)\) (\(a\),\(b\), constants)

where \(z^{-}\mathbf{H}_{v}(z)\) is an entire function of \(z\).

##### Power Series Expansion

\[\mathbf{H}_{v}(z)= (\tfrac{1}{2}z)^{r+1}\sum\limits_{k=0}^{n}\frac{(-1)^{k}(\tfrac{1}{2}z)^{2 k}}{\Gamma(k+\tfrac{3}{2})\Gamma(k+r+\tfrac{3}{2})}\]

1.4 \(\mathbf{H}_{0}(z)= \frac{2}{\pi}\left[z-\frac{z^{3}}{1^{2}.3^{2}}+\frac{z^{5}}{1^{2}.3^{5}.5^{2}}\cdots\right]\)

\[\mathbf{H}_{v}(z)= \frac{2}{\pi}\left[\frac{z^{2}}{1^{2}.3}\frac{z^{4}}{1^{2}.3^{2}.5 }+\frac{z^{6}}{1^{2}.3^{5}.5^{7}}\cdots\right]\]

\[\text{\bf Integral Representations}\]

If \(\mathscr{R}>-\frac{1}{2}\),

\[\mathbf{H}_{v}(z)= \frac{2(\tfrac{3}{2}z)^{r}}{\sqrt{\pi}\,\Gamma(v+\tfrac{1}{2})} \int_{0}^{1}(1-t^{2})^{r-\frac{1}{2}}\sin\,(z\,t)\,dt\]

